    "result_text": "The full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the daily create-limit rule for `POST /api/owners`: once **100 or more** owners already have a `registrationDate` of today, a create request is rejected with **429 Too Many Requests**.\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions, I added:\n\n1. **`RequireDailyLimit`** (`function/owner/`) \u2014 a guard step that counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()` and throws the checked `DailyLimitExceededException` at the limit of 100. Modeled on the existing `RequireCityCapacity` step (runs before the owner is built, so the count reflects owners that already exist).\n\n2. **`DailyLimitExceededException`** (checked, `extends Exception`) \u2014 so it surfaces in the `throws` clause and routes to escalation handling.\n\n3. **`DailyLimitExceededExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds `429` with a `ProblemDetail` body, mirroring the `CityAtCapacityExceptionHandler` (which uses 409).\n\n4. **Escalation YAML** mapping the exception to the handler.\n\n5. Wired a new `dailyLimit` step into `owners.POST.yml` between `capacity` and `build`, under `govern: [ transaction ]` like its neighbours.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` test (create 100, expect the 101st to be `429`) and the full suite pass.",
